X:27
T:Jolly Good Fellow
T:Malbrook
% NFF Book 2024
S:collected from the Nariel Band, 1982-1985, Vic
Z:arranged by Dave De Santi
B:"Music Makes Me Smile", Peter Ellis & Harry Gardner (eds), 2nd edn, 2015, p225
H:A French air and burlesque song that lamented the rumored death of
H:the Duke of Marlborough, John Churchill, at the battle of Malplaquet, 1709.
H:In 1789 this tune was whistled to a group of natives at Sydney Harbour
H:as witnessed by Watkin Tench.
N:Other versions collected in Australia:
N: - by Harry Schaefer MS, Forbes, NSW, as First Set of Quadrilles, 6th Fig, as "We Wont Come Home Until Morning"
